umber of  eyes after throwing two dices  and now i will explain to you the second  way which is how you can calculate it  online with data tab in order to do this  just google data tab click on the  statistics calculator and copy your own  data into this table  then select this tab and click on the  variables you want to analyze  data that recognizes that there are  dependent samples and automatically  calculates a t-test for dependent  samples  you can also choose whether you want to  test an undirected or a directed  hypothesis  further datadeb gives you the hypotheses  and if you scroll down you get the  results  here you can read the p-value if the  p-value is smaller than your defined  significance level for example five  percent  then the null hypothesis is rejected  based on the available data in this case  the p-value is 0.197  which is greater than 0.05  therefore the null hypothesis is  retained  furthermore you can also check the  assumptions and get an interpretation in  words  the score before vacation had lower  values than the score after vacation  a dependent sample status showed that  this difference was not statistically  significant  this results in a p-value of 0.197  which is above the established  significance level of 0.05  therefore the theta's result is not  significant and the null hypothesis is  maintained  this means that it is assumed that both  samples are from the same population  i hope you enjoyed the video if you like  just try data dab it's very easy to use  bye and see you next time  me
 

